        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Boots on the Ground</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/47036.webp" alt="Boots on the Ground" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>[vc_row][vc_column width=&#8221;1/2&#8243;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7881&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221;][/vc_column][vc_column width=&#8221;1/2&#8243;][vc_column_text]</p>
<h3><strong>Here to Lend a Hand </strong></h3>
<div>Tinny represents <strong>all</strong> of Teton Valley&#8217;s hard-working nonprofits. At the Community Foundation, we appreciate the opportunity to help <strong>elevate all sectors </strong>of the nonprofit landscape in Teton Valley. By <strong>supporting the whole</strong>, we ensure that community members always <strong>have access</strong> to ready resources, education, and opportunities.
<p>[/vc_column_text][vc_btn title=&#8221;Donate Now!&#8221; color=&#8221;danger&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; link=&#8221;url:https%3A%2F%2Fcfjh.iphiview.com%2Fcfjh%2FDonorView%2FAccountInformation%2Ftabid%2F495%2Fdispatch%2Faccountselection_id%2410906_hash%241c0c71b9a8078a604dbdfa2c94b19b5566a479d2%2FDefault.aspx|||&#8221;][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]At the <strong>Community Foundation</strong>, we understand the need for a <strong>central support</strong> <strong>system</strong> for local nonprofits. <strong>Providing a hub</strong> for nonprofit staff &amp; board members to <strong>network</strong>, <strong>brainstorm</strong>, and <strong>learn together</strong> through our workshops and roundtables is invaluable for local nonprofit leaders. As a <strong>trusted resource</strong>, we can <strong>strategically</strong> work to elevate the community and further the missions of Teton Valley&#8217;s nonprofits through our Competitive Grant, Youth Philanthropy, and Tin Cup Challenge Programs.[/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]</p>
<div><em>“The support from the Community Foundation over the years has been instrumental in helping Teton Valley Trails and Pathways execute its mission. Whether it be funding through Tin Cup, the competitive grant cycles, or trainings for staff and board, the Community Foundation’s work has undoubtedly improved lives in Teton Valley.” </em>
<div>— Dan Verbaten, Executive Director, Teton Valley Trails &amp; Pathways
<p>[/vc_column_text][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=&#8221;1/2&#8243;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7882&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221;][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=&#8221;1/2&#8243;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7884&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221;][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]</p>
<div><em>“The Community Foundation of Teton Valley is an amazing resource for small nonprofits, helping us gain training and network with other local nonprofit leaders. I’ve attended some great workshops this year. Tin Cup and the Competitive Grant Programs provide Teton Valley Community Recycling with a large part of our budget to make community recycling projects a reality. Thank you for all you do for our community, Community Foundation.&#8221;​</em>
<div>— Iris Saxer, Executive Director, Teton Valley Community Recycling
<p>[/vc_column_text][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=&#8221;1/2&#8243;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7885&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221;][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=&#8221;1/2&#8243;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7883&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221;][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]</p>
<div><em>“The Community Foundation of Teton Valley has been a tremendous support to the Teton Valley Education Foundation. Their Tin Cup efforts literally are the reason why we can spend our time implementing our programs rather than fundraising for operating dollars. They are one of only a handful of Foundations that will support the basics such as salaries, insurance, postage&#8230;the lifeblood of an organization. Then to have the added benefit of applying for grants to kick start a new program is incredible. I can honestly say that we would not be where we are today, a thriving nonprofit, if not for the CFTV. Thank you from the bottom of our hearts!”​</em>
<div>— Pam Walker, Executive Director, Education Foundation of Teton Valley
<p>[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]<strong>Our community</strong> is incredibly lucky to have so many successful nonprofits at work on our behalf. Through their dedication local community members, animals, and land receive <strong>necessary care</strong> and <strong>amazing opportunities</strong> that allow our community to <strong>thrive</strong> across all sectors: Education, Civic &amp; Service, Health &amp; Human Services, Animal rescue, Conservation &amp; Environment, Sports &amp; Recreation, and Arts &amp; Culture.[/vc_column_text][vc_separator][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=&#8221;1/2&#8243;][vc_column_text]</p>
<h3><strong>Community Counts!</strong></h3>
<div>Tinny thrives when we all come together to support one another.<strong> </strong>The Community Foundation&#8217;s <strong>Tin Cup Challenge</strong> brings <strong>giving to the forefront</strong> of our community, makes <strong>donating easy</strong>, <strong>encourages philanthropy, </strong>and <strong>elevates lives </strong>for all. Consider supporting Tinny&#8217;s efforts with a <strong>direct donation</strong> to the <strong>Community Foundation</strong> to ensure a fresh, full cup of Tin Cup Funds for everyone, annually.
<p>[/vc_column_text][vc_btn title=&#8221;Donate Now!&#8221; color=&#8221;danger&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; link=&#8221;url:https%3A%2F%2Fcfjh.iphiview.com%2Fcfjh%2FDonorView%2FAccountInformation%2Ftabid%2F495%2Fdispatch%2Faccountselection_id%2410906_hash%241c0c71b9a8078a604dbdfa2c94b19b5566a479d2%2FDefault.aspx|||&#8221;][/vc_column][vc_column width=&#8221;1/2&#8243;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7864&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221;][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]</p>
<h3><span><strong>Giving Period ends Friday, July 26th at 5pm.</strong></span></h3>
<p>[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]</p>
